    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Gaps in the date ranges of consecutive blng__FinancePeriod__c records on the same finance book.
Why it matters: Postings whose date falls in a gap have nowhere to land — they fail or land in a suspense bucket. Auditors flag period gaps as a material control weakness.
Suppress a finding: only when a gap is deliberate (company was dormant, no postings expected) and documented for audit.
Disable the detector: only if your org accepts period gaps by design. Most orgs should leave this on.</value></values>
